WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.720
Same procedure.

2
00:00:00.790 --> 00:00:01.340
Same patient.

3
00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:02.120
A different building.

4
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:04.660
Office.

5
00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:05.670
Surgery center.

6
00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:07.040
Hospital outpatient.

7
00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:08.960
One procedure.

8
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.100
One case.

9
00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:12.960
Medicare's own published rates.

10
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:16.590
Office to hospital, plus one hundred sixty eight percent.

11
00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:19.370
The building is the price.

12
00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:23.880
Most health plans must file their contracted rates.

13
00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.200
The files are public.

14
00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:26.920
And huge.

15
00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:30.790
Almost nobody on the buying side opens one.

16
00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:32.980
We read them.

17
00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:34.990
That is the whole company.

18
00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:41.130
A sample too thin gets a refusal, not a number.

19
00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:46.250
The first bad number you hand a chief financial officer is the last one they trust.

20
00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:50.100
Brokers bring the page to the renewal table.

21
00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:53.190
General agencies hand it to every producer.

22
00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:57.750
Self-funded employers weigh one building against the next.

23
00:00:57.730 --> 00:01:00.890
Health plans see their filed rates beside the market.

24
00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:03.900
One flat fee.

25
00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:05.450
Never a share of anything.

26
00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:08.480
Bring a procedure and a place.

27
00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:09.251
The door is open.
